signed that contract, that agreement by Laguerreira, he's with the nation of France. So therefore,

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:37.140
in France, which in France, this agreement was with a French nation.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:45.140
And the people who signed the agreement are today alive or not alive. You make the covenant,

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:52.140
He got the agreement, the alliance with England, France, Germany, wherever. And this is...

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:57.140
And this is...

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:03.140
So therefore, we have two covenants, and two of them precious and interrelated, one with the other.

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:09.140
I have a personal thing. Yes, I am going, or not going to go get up this morning for Seri Hord.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.140
That's a very personal thing. Yes. A very, very personal thing.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:42.140
I want to do this, I want to do that, I don't want to do this, I want to do this, I don't want to do this, I want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this, I don't want to do this

00:14:42.140 --> 00:15:02.280
But that is the policy of America. I am an American. I will do that. You know, I will defend the interests of America. Is it right that America is a pro-regulist? I don't know. I'm not too sure. But America, the President, the Senate, had decided this. I am going to follow what America says.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:14.140
And the same thing exactly is with Han Israel, these two dimensions, you know, the personal, that is Sinai, and then there is the natural. And what does it mean, Nusavim?

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:28.140
An interesting word, nsabim, means you are in the present. Let me explain. In Yom Kippur, it says,

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:32.140
لَعُلَامَ اَدُنَاءَ لِبَرْخَانِ صَافَ الشَّمَاءِ

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.140
نَصَافَ

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.140
Your word is نَصَافَ

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:40.140
The word is is نَصَافَ

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:44.140
And you are, in the plural, نَصَابِين

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.140
نَصَافَ نَصَابِين

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:49.140
It's a very important thing.

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:57.140
We are, because we are humans, we always think in the frame of time and space.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:16.960
I said, we will die at this way someday, this time, and so on. And therefore you assume that when the time lapses, that word, that word I said to you, it was yesterday, it was an hour ago. And it lapses with the time, you know.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:22.460
But God is not standing this way. When God says, for instance,

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:25.460
Anokhi Adonai Elohecha

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:31.460
He's saying it just now, right now He's saying Anokhi Adonai Elohecha

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.460
So it's speaking about time.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:38.460
The whole concept of time does not apply to the word of God

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:42.960
that He said in the both of them used to go over like this.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:48.960
The world of God is speaking to us now.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.960
Some people say, why God didn't say again,

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.960
man said, his self is naked now.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:17:01.960
There is no chronology that applies to the world of God.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.960
There is no time in the world of God.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.960
The same thing,

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:20.960
At that moment, we said we accept this national obligation. I do it, I don't agree with that.

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:28.960
But this is the way that I'm going to go and follow through. I'm a member of the Jewish nation.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:49.940
I'm going to do it. This is with all of us. We show him, everybody, from the highest to the lowest, from the child to the grown-up, a male, female. We are, and that event is the sub.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:57.940
I don't like the word eternal, but I would say timeless, or I would say perennial.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:07.940
It's perennially present, it's always present. And then in that sense, you can understand now what is the society of the Buddha.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:23.940
I wanted to say this, the two dimensions that we live in, we may be sure of this or that, but if we are in a world which is collectively,

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:41.940
Now, before I want to say something. We made as a nation a contract with God. Any contract that you make, it has clauses. And what happened with you? You fought. You don't pay any time.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:49.760
Well, you're going to be fined, I don't know, $5,000 a day, or $500 a day, or $50 a day, or $5 a day.

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.040
This and this and that.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:52.320
They are exactly the same.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:56.560
Exactly the contract tells you what are the liabilities.

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:05.980
Yes, as I use it when I write in Hebrew, I say that a contract constructs, builds obligations.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.000
That's what that contract is.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.680
And that stipulates what the consequences are.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:21.940
Now, if you pay attention, the Barakhot and the Keralot, yes, are all to do with earthly problems, yes.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:34.940
This would happen, Bar-Miran would distort, the other, you know, people that would do Bar-Miran would be spoiled or, you know, successful.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:38.940
What does it mean? At the national dimension.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:43.940
There is berakhod in kira lor in this world.

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:48.940
Are we going to be successful in this world as a nation?

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:55.940
The individual thinks for Allah, what I put up in the name, or don't put up in the name,

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.940
the consequences are automatically in Allah.

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:07.940
The national dimension, the consequences are material in this world.

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:13.940
And therefore, before you accept the covenant, this national covenant with God,

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:22.940
God tells you exactly what are the liabilities and what are the pluses of this covenant.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:29.940
You see? And let me explain something a little bit more than that.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.940
We are in galut.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:36.940
Where the heck? God destroy the metamethas.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:42.940
Galut is not because somebody didn't put the healing.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:46.940
It's not because somebody didn't eat coffee or whatever the issue is.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:57.940
simply, that person doesn't know the truth. He has a vacuum in his knowledge, and everybody is saying,

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:07.940
Kacher, the Kacher, Rabbi Shlomo Yerberga, the great Chacham from Seville, he says everybody knows the Spanish, nobody speaks in Spanish.

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:24.940
Nobody, nobody. So why were they exactly from Spain, he says. Because we had, he doesn't use the word imbeciles, but something close to the word imbeciles for political leaders.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:32.940
The sin was a political sin. Political sin is not that we voted for the democracy or the republic.

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:39.940
It is that we do not know how to administer our political affairs, our affairs as a nation.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:44.940
Yes? The Aval is a political Aval. Yes?

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:48.940
Everybody said, Miha, everybody is Shom Shabbat, everybody ate kosher.

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:55.440
If you did not want to eat kosher, you say, yeah, no need to eat not kosher.

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:57.440
Whatever you want to eat, not kosher.

00:21:57.440 --> 00:22:01.440
You can't be Mechad Shabbat if you want to be Mechad Shabbat.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:03.440
Everybody should be Shabbat Shabbat.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:07.440
So that was everybody who went to Bitta Knesset.

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:09.440
They didn't have any other place to go.

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:11.440
So they went to Bitta Knesset.

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:13.440
Everybody stuck in because it was the problem.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.440
That was not the problem.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:27.440
The flaw, the sin of Galut is not because of the Berit in Sinai, but because of the Berit in Moab.

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:33.440
The Berit in Moab tells you exactly what happened to us in history.

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:38.440
What happened to us in history is not written in the Berit of Sinai. It's the Berit of Moab.

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:46.440
We failed as a political entity. We did not take wise, intelligent, political decisions.

00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:54.440
I want to tell you a fantastic story. When I was a young boy, I came to Jerusalem, I was studying in Leipzig, Yishua.

00:22:54.440 --> 00:23:01.440
And I became friendly with my friend, somebody, I don't remember who his last name was, Fink or Finkel.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:14.440
And he told me a story. I will never, never, never forget that story. I remember in Spain, he was a very, very well-mannered, very nice, sweet young man.

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:22.440
And he would get me to be friendly because he came to this country, to America via Uruguay, Paraguay, and those countries.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:52.420
And he told me what happened. He was in the Shoah, in Germany or he was in Belgium, today Belgium. And he says he remembered that he was, he, his younger brother and his father and mother, they were in a train taking them to one of those famous institutions.

00:23:52.440 --> 00:24:08.440
How did they save? The father and mother, the train stopped for something, they got off the train with the children.

00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:20.440
Then they walked to Paraguayan council, they paid $500 for each one, they always saved.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:35.440
The problem, part of the problem was that the people just didn't get off the train. They didn't get off the train. This is one of the... didn't get off the train.

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:43.440
Political, faulty political leadership. If they say, if the leadership says, we don't know how to save you.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:25:05.080
Now I'm sorry if you cannot say with two people in one hand, try to save yourself and your own. We have small choices of how we save. But what I'm trying to say is the flaw or the sin is a political sin. It's poor political leadership.

00:25:05.080 --> 00:25:11.080
That is what Bishop Ramon Ibn Berga in the famous book, Sheveti Ulam, tried to do in Musfet.

00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:17.080
Has nothing to do with Kashrut. Nothing to do. We should keep our proposal. We made a covenant with God.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:23.080
That's a personal covenant. But as a nation, we have to know how to behave as a nation.

00:25:23.080 --> 00:25:31.080
I once, I had a friend of mine, Arab Shalom, Mr. Dwayne, Dr. Dwayne, I don't know if you remember him.

00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:38.080
So Dr. Dweck, he told me something very interesting.

00:25:38.080 --> 00:25:44.080
That he was somehow connected with the Air Force.

00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:47.080
And he was a doctor, something to do with the Air Force.

00:25:47.080 --> 00:25:52.080
And he once told me something very, very profound.

00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:56.080
He asked the people of the Air Force,

00:25:56.080 --> 00:26:03.080
how the Israeli Air Force fares compared to the American Air Force.

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:08.080
And the answer was for me illuminating.

00:26:08.080 --> 00:26:13.080
It says one and one, an Israeli versus an American,

00:26:13.080 --> 00:26:16.080
I mean in those days, I'm talking 20, 30 years ago,

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:18.080
the Israeli would beat the Americans.

00:26:18.080 --> 00:26:21.080
One pilot, one plane against another plane.

00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:40.520
But if they have a like 30 against 30, you know, the Americans will beat the Israelis. And that is the problem. It is very interesting problem. We do not know how to act as a team. We do not know how to act as a team. Yes?

00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:51.520
A lot of people are basketball, one-on-one, they beat you, but they do not know how to develop a strategy as a team.

00:26:51.520 --> 00:27:04.520
And the problem that we have is that the head coach or head coach, I don't know, are dumb.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:17.680
I'm dumb, that's the word, dumb, dumb, dumb, dumb, dumb, stupid, dumb, dumb.

00:27:19.680 --> 00:27:25.860
Individuals are great, but what happens when you have to fight a team?

00:27:27.200 --> 00:27:30.060
You will know how to respond, but this is interesting.

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:55.020
So anyhow, I go to the next step. I will let everybody express their opinion. But again, we have two governments. We have two lives. I want to say to some of you, this sounds horrendous and really, it should not be accepted.

00:27:55.020 --> 00:28:12.020
I've written in my book in the shadow of history. There were some, you know that in Spain and Portugal, the people who converted. And they were called, you know what they called themselves? The people of the nation.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:28.020
Only nation. And because they believe that although the religious aspect of Judaism, they could no longer ascertain,

00:28:28.020 --> 00:28:36.020
because they could not, because they could not be Shabbat in Kachar, in Portugal or Spain, but they were members of the Jewish nation.

00:28:36.020 --> 00:28:53.020
And I bring a dialer, the one who was from somewhere in Brazil, in 1600s. And the guy says, yes, I'm a member of the nation and we're there. The Mashiach will come, he will redeem me.

00:28:53.020 --> 00:29:02.020
So they saw the Mashiach as the proper figure. Mashiach is, as Abraham said, a political leader.

00:29:02.020 --> 00:29:12.020
He is a political leader who is going to resuscitate not the individuals of Israel, but the nation of Israel.

00:29:12.020 --> 00:29:23.020
You know, we got to live in a Jewish nation. Yes? And we want to have political unity among ourselves.

00:29:23.020 --> 00:29:31.020
That is the Mashiach. The Mashiach has nothing to do with the Amapá. The Mashiach has nothing to do with the Amazigh.

00:29:31.020 --> 00:29:38.020
The Mashiach is the... you know, the Mashiach is not to make you put a pin in your... that's not the question. The Mashiach does this.

00:29:38.020 --> 00:29:47.020
Now, I want to add one word more and then I let you speak or ask me or whatever, just debate whatever you want.

00:29:47.020 --> 00:29:57.020
I want to add one word. The word Mashiach is a political term. It's a political term. It's not a religious term. It's a political term.

00:29:57.020 --> 00:30:16.220
What you do is that a king, whenever he is going to be appointed as such, there is a ceremony. In Jewish tradition, the king is to be appointed by the Sanhedrin because we are a constitutional state.

00:30:16.220 --> 00:30:24.220
He has the Sanhedrin, he is a Kenim of Israel, the Sanhedrin, and he will be anointed.

00:30:24.220 --> 00:30:40.220
He is going to be our political man because we as Jews choose that.

00:30:40.220 --> 00:31:01.280
That is the ceremony that is going to ascertain that we are doing it as Jewish people. We are not going to appoint them according to the tradition say of Belgium or the Prince of Bacchus. We are going to do it according to our ways.

00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:21.880
Ours. Our king is going to be anointed in our way. It's going to be a continuation of an old tradition. Yes? And we are not going to surrender our own particularities as a nation. Yes?

00:31:21.880 --> 00:31:28.080
I mean, nobody would say, well, yes, I will make an alliance with you, England,

00:31:28.580 --> 00:31:31.880
on condition that you normally speak with a British accent.

00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:33.180
Well, that is the England.

00:31:33.860 --> 00:31:36.120
In England, they speak with a British accent.

00:31:36.680 --> 00:31:36.860
Yes?

00:31:37.400 --> 00:31:40.380
So, that is our style, that's our line.

00:31:40.760 --> 00:31:41.980
That's the way we see things.

00:31:41.980 --> 00:31:47.420
You have to preserve that uniqueness.

00:31:47.420 --> 00:32:01.540
And again, the Mashinah is going to be a Jewish political leader because we as a Jewish nation want to install him as such.

00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:03.040
That's all.

00:32:04.660 --> 00:32:08.920
So I'm stopping here.

00:32:09.740 --> 00:32:13.140
Questions, answers, remarks, criticisms?

00:32:13.140 --> 00:32:15.840
mentioned a few weeks ago

00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:17.940
there was a Jew that passed away

00:32:17.940 --> 00:32:20.060
in the 1940s

00:32:20.060 --> 00:32:21.680
he got his name, Morris

00:32:21.680 --> 00:32:22.540
I gave you the article

00:32:22.540 --> 00:32:25.880
what was the name of that person that I gave you

00:32:25.880 --> 00:32:27.180
that passed away

00:32:27.180 --> 00:32:28.920
we read it

00:32:28.920 --> 00:32:30.940
in the 1940s

00:32:30.940 --> 00:32:33.860
he was an activist but he told

00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:36.060
the Jews what was going on in Germany

00:32:36.060 --> 00:32:36.740
in America

00:32:36.740 --> 00:32:38.500
he told everybody

00:32:38.500 --> 00:32:40.680
nobody would listen

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:42.900
and he did many things

00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:45.600
to try to open the people's eyes.

00:32:46.320 --> 00:32:47.920
I forgot his name. I have the article home.

00:32:48.360 --> 00:32:51.880
Well, I mean, Mr. Faker, just walk out from the train.

00:32:52.180 --> 00:32:54.920
Yeah, but it's hard to do that when you don't have a sovereign state

00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:57.580
and you don't have leadership that is not, you know...

00:32:57.580 --> 00:32:59.320
That's true. However...

00:32:59.320 --> 00:33:00.940
So when you have a sovereign state, you're able to do...

00:33:00.940 --> 00:33:07.160
Fine, fine. But I just want to say, this person had $500 for each one of these.

00:33:07.160 --> 00:33:11.640
He walked with the $500 with the Paraguayan consulate.

00:33:11.640 --> 00:33:13.120
He gave $500 for it.

00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:13.880
He got the visa.

00:33:14.680 --> 00:33:14.900
Yes.

00:33:15.480 --> 00:33:18.140
I mean, not everybody would have been able to save himself.

00:33:18.420 --> 00:33:21.380
Some people just walk out of the train.

00:33:22.200 --> 00:33:23.360
I mean, walk out.

00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:27.020
I say to myself, but don't quote me.

00:33:27.120 --> 00:33:29.360
If you quote me, I'm going to say that this was false.

00:33:30.940 --> 00:33:35.300
I say that the miracle was not that he walked out of the train.

00:33:36.400 --> 00:33:41.540
The miracle was that there were other people like the medics and Yossi Sarit and Yossi.

00:33:41.640 --> 00:33:46.040
is that it's tell them the couple's in the, they tell, look at you, time to go out.

00:33:46.040 --> 00:33:49.740
That is the great miracle. We have to recognize that the problem

00:33:49.740 --> 00:33:53.040
lies not with the, with the, with the boy, but lies,

00:33:53.040 --> 00:33:56.640
in many cases, within ourselves. We are,

00:33:56.640 --> 00:34:00.240
I mean, there's our worst, worst, worst

00:34:00.240 --> 00:34:03.640
enemies. And, but there is no reason

00:34:03.640 --> 00:34:09.440
why Mr. Fink, I get, Fink, I forget, I forget his name,

00:34:09.440 --> 00:34:11.400
of this young boy,

00:34:11.640 --> 00:34:12.120
young boy,

00:34:12.200 --> 00:34:14.240
my father right now,

00:34:15.180 --> 00:34:16.800
just walk out,

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:18.120
just walk out of the train,

00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:19.040
just walk out,

00:34:19.720 --> 00:34:20.020
you know,

00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:20.780
and,

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:24.520
but the problem is that we are beguiled

00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:27.040
by stupid leaders,

00:34:28.020 --> 00:34:31.400
people who are mentally incompetent,

00:34:32.160 --> 00:34:33.680
they are failures,

00:34:34.920 --> 00:34:35.700
failures,

00:34:36.420 --> 00:34:36.700
yes,

00:34:37.040 --> 00:34:37.600
failures,

00:34:37.600 --> 00:34:56.040
And we are walking like a sheep, possibly a wolf, a shepherd. And that is a problem. And I want to say something on behalf of the Separatists. We're not better than anybody else.

00:34:56.040 --> 00:35:16.040
But during the war, and people do not understand this, the same Vichy government that was sending people in France to the Adams was in Morocco.

00:35:16.040 --> 00:35:20.040
And there are for whatever reasons, not the Jews touched.

00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:26.040
Well, they say to some Jews, where but where, they were let them die for this.

00:35:26.040 --> 00:35:33.040
What happened? And this is something which is very important.

00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:43.040
We were not stupid to believe that when the Nazi says we want to kill you, and they shoot at you,

00:35:43.040 --> 00:35:59.300
And by a miracle they missed the bullet at three minutes. They are really good people. And therefore the Jews in Morocco, they play the right cards, they bribe the right persons, and nobody was touched.

00:35:59.300 --> 00:36:15.280
The same Mishi government was in Lebanon. Yes, nothing happened. Why? The Jews, part of being a good leader is not to be stupid. And therefore, you have to accept the performance as well.

00:36:15.280 --> 00:36:20.280
I remember there was a Hakam, very nice, ala b'shalom Rabbi Yosef Tamar.

00:36:20.280 --> 00:36:28.280
And I know him very well now, a book of his, you got, Maurice you got the book, wonderful Hakam.

00:36:28.280 --> 00:36:38.280
He told me, when there was a problem, anti-Semitism was always alive in the world.

00:36:38.280 --> 00:37:08.280
So why he was 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to be 11 and having to

00:37:08.280 --> 00:37:34.060
You don't mean that. You think that they are actually mean it? You know? We didn't think that way. We acted. And the net result was that there were very few victims. But thank God as a whole, I'm not saying all over, but there was an attempt at least to cope with the situation.

00:37:34.060 --> 00:37:39.220
So, again, this is the whole notion of political Teshuva,

00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:41.440
when we're talking about Teshuva and Teshuva,

00:37:41.680 --> 00:37:43.760
and Sefer Haim, what does it mean?

00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:47.780
We have to have some questions or something.

00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:55.480
Was Ibn Jarrah the first one to point out the distinction between the two Berithas?

00:37:55.700 --> 00:37:57.400
No, first of all, he doesn't say it.

00:37:57.480 --> 00:37:59.280
I am the one who wrote it.

00:37:59.520 --> 00:38:02.300
The first person who wrote this is me.

00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:09.300
But he speaks about the political thing and I am the one who explains what does it mean.

00:38:09.300 --> 00:38:19.300
The statements on how to give a thing in the heart of the world, are they, is karet the punishment for all of those things on a national level?

00:38:19.300 --> 00:38:25.300
No. Karet, they don't mention they are karet. It doesn't say karet. Karet is at the personal level.

00:38:25.300 --> 00:38:26.300
Karet is personal.

00:38:26.300 --> 00:38:27.300
It's personal.

00:38:27.300 --> 00:38:35.500
But you leave, but you're out, you don't necessarily have to die or not have that, from what I understood, but you get cut off from the national...

00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:43.420
That's right. You don't, the person doesn't get this protection that God awards to the people.

00:38:43.980 --> 00:38:52.340
And I was, since I personally betrayed the nation, then I'm a little bit alienated. I alienated myself.

00:38:53.540 --> 00:38:55.620
Karet means really alienation.

00:38:55.620 --> 00:39:11.780
But should it all, should, you know, using your model as a national, as a national stipulation that you're making on a national level, not on a personal level, shouldn't Qaris be the punishment for those?

00:39:12.820 --> 00:39:12.980
No.

00:39:14.520 --> 00:39:20.120
What does it mean, cursed? What does it mean? What does it mean? You're out of the nation?

00:39:20.120 --> 00:39:22.120
or does it work?

00:39:22.120 --> 00:39:24.120
The nation will, that's what it says even at the end,

00:39:24.120 --> 00:39:28.120
that even when you're going to punish the nation,

00:39:28.120 --> 00:39:32.120
you're going to punish the Galud, this,

00:39:32.120 --> 00:39:34.120
but you always, as I explained,

00:39:34.120 --> 00:39:36.120
when I was a child,

00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:38.120
now I consider myself a dad,

00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:40.120
I was 21 years old when I wrote a book

00:39:40.120 --> 00:39:42.120
called the Spirituai Lacuia.

00:39:42.120 --> 00:39:46.120
I wrote it for, in Spain,

00:39:46.120 --> 00:39:47.460
21.

00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:49.800
Amplified without

00:39:49.800 --> 00:39:50.200
principle.

00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:55.900
The punishment

00:39:55.900 --> 00:39:57.900
is very interesting. You have to have a legal

00:39:57.900 --> 00:40:00.020
mind for that. You're not going to have a legal mind

00:40:00.020 --> 00:40:00.900
then. He said,

00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:03.580
when you have sanctions

00:40:03.580 --> 00:40:04.800
in a contract,

00:40:05.480 --> 00:40:07.000
sanctions of a contract,

00:40:08.300 --> 00:40:09.880
implied that the contract

00:40:09.880 --> 00:40:10.460
is valid,

00:40:11.560 --> 00:40:13.820
God never would dissolve the contract

00:40:13.820 --> 00:40:15.920
with Israel. The fact that

00:40:15.920 --> 00:40:23.680
punishes us means that the contract is valid forever and ever and ever. We suffer, we pay the price.

00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:29.120
Yes? But even if He's going to send you to the ends of the world and so on,

00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:36.400
and He's going to bring you back to the ends of Israel, He's going to color you again,

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:43.520
and you want to be a god. There is a punishment. But the punishment, see, as a matter of fact,

00:40:43.520 --> 00:40:47.580
I explained then, that the word punishment, this kind of

00:40:47.580 --> 00:40:51.700
word in Hebrew, means punishment, not as we say

00:40:51.700 --> 00:40:55.740
it in English, but rather we read sanctions. Because sanctions

00:40:55.740 --> 00:40:59.460
means that a contract is valid. It's not punishment

00:40:59.460 --> 00:41:03.300
that I'm punching you on the nose because I don't like you. No, these are the sanctions

00:41:03.300 --> 00:41:07.600
stipulated in the contract. So therefore when the punishment comes, or the sanctions

00:41:07.600 --> 00:41:11.620
come, that is another word in which God is

00:41:11.620 --> 00:41:14.620
saying the contract is valid.

00:41:14.620 --> 00:41:23.460
This contract is valid forever.

00:41:24.220 --> 00:41:24.440
Yes?

00:41:24.800 --> 00:41:25.680
And therefore,

00:41:25.820 --> 00:41:26.820
there will be punishment.

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:30.580
We are talking about specific sanctions.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:32.560
Sanctions rather than punishment.

00:41:32.940 --> 00:41:35.020
Now, karek is something personal.

00:41:35.840 --> 00:41:37.560
I did something,

00:41:38.380 --> 00:41:39.920
and therefore this is affecting

00:41:39.920 --> 00:41:44.080
God would say, no, no, no, you are not like everybody else.

00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:47.080
You know?

00:41:47.080 --> 00:41:53.080
And, but you could repent, but that's a personal thing.

00:41:53.080 --> 00:41:55.080
It's a personal thing.

00:41:55.080 --> 00:41:57.080
It's a personal thing.

00:41:57.080 --> 00:42:01.080
You were saying that Moshiach is a political entity,

00:42:01.080 --> 00:42:06.080
and it has to do, it's based in this world.

00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:14.080
How do you, how do you, what dimension does the law and halakha and everything have to do with that?

00:42:14.080 --> 00:42:25.080
We are, first and foremost, a constitutional nation. We have a constitution. The constitution is called Torah.

00:42:25.080 --> 00:42:32.080
That is our constitution. The Torah, like any constitution, needs a body that interprets it.

00:42:32.080 --> 00:42:43.080
in America is called the Supreme Court, in Jewish it's called Sanhedrin. Sanhedrin interprets the constitution of Am Yisrael.

00:42:43.080 --> 00:42:56.080
Yes? Now, that is Halakha, is the law, which is the result of the Sanhedrin interpretation of the constitution of Am Yisrael.

00:42:56.080 --> 00:43:09.080
Now, the monarch, the Jewish monarch, I don't like the word monarch, the Jewish political leader, whatever, I don't, maybe I should think about some other sovereign, not even a sovereign, I don't like to call sovereign.

00:43:09.080 --> 00:43:18.080
But anyhow, Mashiach. Mashiach is a person, for us, is going to upheld the constitutional himself.

00:43:18.080 --> 00:43:31.080
is a constitutional monarch, or whatever you want to call it. Yes, it's a constitutional monarch. Yes. And therefore, the law is going to be the law of Israel. Yes.

00:43:31.080 --> 00:43:45.080
And not the law of the Israeli state, which is, I don't know where it is. But it's the law of the Jewish people. Yes. And it's going to be interpreted and so on.

00:43:45.080 --> 00:43:52.580
like the Arabs and the Indians will interpret our Constitution just like the U.S. Supreme Court

00:43:52.580 --> 00:43:57.080
interprets the Constitution of the nation of America.

00:43:57.080 --> 00:44:00.580
What do you mean by not a Jewish state? Is that right?

00:44:00.580 --> 00:44:10.580
It's that they... when they say that this is a Jewish state, you have to have a sense of humor.

00:44:15.080 --> 00:44:24.120
But they're still fighting for us.

00:44:24.240 --> 00:44:25.860
They are not fighting for us.

00:44:26.380 --> 00:44:27.940
I don't think that there's such a...

00:44:27.940 --> 00:44:29.780
You have to remember that many of them,

00:44:30.340 --> 00:44:33.460
if they would come to America, many of these people,

00:44:33.460 --> 00:44:37.780
they will not be able to pass the test

00:44:37.780 --> 00:44:43.640
to qualify as a manager of a small McDonald's

00:44:43.640 --> 00:44:49.640
in a small town of a small state of this United States.

00:44:49.640 --> 00:44:51.640
It's a fact.

00:44:51.640 --> 00:44:59.640
The closer to the word imbecile is an Israeli political leader.

00:44:59.640 --> 00:45:03.640
It's just imbeciles.

00:45:03.640 --> 00:45:07.640
I compare this to...

00:45:07.640 --> 00:45:18.640
You remember the story, beautiful story, in which Belaam faces an angel and then the donkey speaks.

00:45:18.640 --> 00:45:22.640
Now, if you pay attention, the donkey speaks a beautiful Hebrew.

00:45:26.640 --> 00:45:34.640
And I say, suppose somebody says, on the basis of this Hebrew, would you give a chair of Hebrew to this donkey?

00:45:34.640 --> 00:45:43.640
No. Because a donkey is a donkey, it happens to be God Almighty put words in this donkey.

00:45:43.640 --> 00:45:53.640
So, same thing with the wars and the battles of Israel. I don't think that none of the Syrians could shoot a straight arrow.

00:45:53.640 --> 00:45:59.640
It's the miracles of God. Just talk to this God. You see, they don't know where they are coming and going.

00:45:59.640 --> 00:46:04.640
This is God acting through the aton of the an.

00:46:04.640 --> 00:46:07.640
Nothing good, nothing good.

00:46:07.640 --> 00:46:13.640
You will not become to have them as your partner.

00:46:13.640 --> 00:46:19.640
Good people in this day and year.

00:46:19.640 --> 00:46:24.640
Now you say, well, this guy had 500 million dollars.

00:46:24.640 --> 00:46:33.040
true. But his father left him five hundred billion dollars. He squandered the money through

00:46:33.040 --> 00:46:39.280
this, and this, and that, doesn't mean anything. You know? They squandered every single miracle

00:46:39.280 --> 00:46:49.280
of God, they just squandered it. I don't have no respect for them, for these people. I like

00:46:49.280 --> 00:46:55.280
And I love in the wonderful the people of Israel at the lower edges.

00:46:55.280 --> 00:47:06.280
But those who are on the so-called, what I call the Israeli oligarchy, yes, I'm not to, I don't...

00:47:06.280 --> 00:47:10.280
I'm having an open-ended question, I apologize.

00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:13.280
But we're speaking about the State of Israel.

00:47:13.280 --> 00:47:17.280
The State of Israel by and large comes from a political liberal philosophy,

00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:23.440
go back to Descartes, Spinoza, not, again, what you're saying about the Jewish political tradition.

00:47:23.440 --> 00:47:31.560
How does one now, and you write extensively about Khakamim from the Sephardi tradition in the 19th century,

00:47:32.180 --> 00:47:33.420
that had a different philosophy.

00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:40.500
How does one move through the 20th century to today, when obviously many bad things are happening?

00:47:41.280 --> 00:47:43.740
How do you then look at it politically?

00:47:43.740 --> 00:48:00.040
The problem with Israel is that people came to Israel. First of all, Israel was never empty. And it's not true the story that there were swamps and these guys, they were full of mosquitoes.

00:48:00.040 --> 00:48:09.040
This guy, they wouldn't do anything. They were just bombs. Many of them were just bombs. And just bombs. Bombs.

00:48:09.040 --> 00:48:17.040
They got money from the Jewish people and maybe they got some Arabs to clear the swamps and so on. They wouldn't do anything. I don't believe they did anything.

00:48:17.040 --> 00:48:20.940
I'm sorry to interrupt. The story of the swamp at Hula.

00:48:21.220 --> 00:48:21.520
Yes.

00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:28.180
And there's a movie about it, that the Yemenites drained the entire swamp,

00:48:28.920 --> 00:48:30.120
and they made a documentary.

00:48:30.460 --> 00:48:35.300
When you go on a tour of the Kinere today, it's not mentioned.

00:48:35.480 --> 00:48:39.360
The Yemenites were thrown out of the settlement, and all explanation was brought in.

00:48:39.360 --> 00:48:41.560
All right. So that's part of the truth of this.

00:48:41.720 --> 00:48:46.880
So the whole thing is fake.

00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:55.040
Now most of these people, and it's incorrect for me to say that, most of the people with whom I am familiar,

00:48:55.040 --> 00:49:04.040
Stoic and so on, they were people that had no relationship with Judaism whatsoever. None. Zero. Zero.

00:49:04.040 --> 00:49:14.040
It's just like this guy, I knew his name, I hope I'm not, do you remember this guy from Argentina many years ago

00:49:14.040 --> 00:49:34.040
who was a newspaper person, Timmerman. Timmerman was a person belonging to a group in Argentina of Jews who do not circumcise their children.

00:49:34.040 --> 00:49:50.040
They have absolutely no relationship at all with Judaism. None. Zero.

00:49:50.040 --> 00:49:54.040
With Judaism or with the land of Israel. Yes?

00:49:54.040 --> 00:49:57.040
There were actually, there were socialist Jews.

00:49:57.040 --> 00:50:01.040
And there is a fantastic story about them that we know.

00:50:01.040 --> 00:50:16.040
we know there's somebody by the name of Merleman, an Argentinian, very intelligent rabbi who lives in Chicago today, by the name of Merleman, wrote the history of the Jews in Argentina.

00:50:16.040 --> 00:50:32.420
And he has about this kind of people. Absolutely none whatsoever. They have a school, a school in Ash'etina, a Jewish school. It's Yiddish, they don't teach Hebrew. And it's called Yodlamet Beret School, in which it's open in Yom Kippur.

00:50:32.420 --> 00:50:41.420
Right? Right? It's all being done by people. Now, this person had zero relationship with anything Jewish.

00:50:41.420 --> 00:50:47.420
And he was against the government. When the government attacked him, all of a sudden he becomes Jewish.

00:50:47.420 --> 00:50:55.420
Yes? And that was we, Jewish people, we have Rahmanin, we have the compassion and so on, we help them.

00:50:55.420 --> 00:50:58.820
But he became Jewish out of convenience.

00:50:58.820 --> 00:51:05.680
Most of those early Zionists, they were Jews out of convenience.

00:51:05.680 --> 00:51:06.480
Yes.

00:51:06.480 --> 00:51:11.540
And they exploited our good faith for naivete.

00:51:11.540 --> 00:51:14.220
And they took over.

00:51:14.220 --> 00:51:15.860
They took over.

00:51:15.860 --> 00:51:19.780
But they came and they settled the land.

00:51:19.780 --> 00:51:20.820
They didn't settle the land.

00:51:20.820 --> 00:51:21.820
That's not true.

00:51:21.820 --> 00:51:25.400
People were, I mean, going back to, let's say, 1492,

00:51:25.400 --> 00:51:29.800
you have the, you have Abarbanel and all the messianic type of...

00:51:29.800 --> 00:51:31.900
No, no, no, Abarbanel was a good politician.

00:51:32.120 --> 00:51:33.500
He was a political leader.

00:51:33.520 --> 00:51:35.740
But I'm saying, I mean, you can't sit home and pray for...

00:51:35.740 --> 00:51:36.840
No, no, they didn't come here and pray.

00:51:37.100 --> 00:51:39.660
As a matter of fact, no, we are wrong.

00:51:39.920 --> 00:51:42.740
I think in a year or two from now, God willing,

00:51:43.200 --> 00:51:44.500
I'm going to publish a documentation.

00:51:45.220 --> 00:51:48.740
The Jews in Israel...

00:51:49.380 --> 00:51:50.820
Why didn't they go to Israel?

00:51:52.260 --> 00:51:53.700
First of all, they did.

00:51:53.700 --> 00:52:15.300
And by the way, very interesting thing, Safed, Yerushalayim, Tiberias, Hebron, they were populated and revived by the Jews who came from Spain, by the Sephardim.

00:52:15.300 --> 00:52:16.300
Yes?

00:52:16.300 --> 00:52:22.300
No, no, not only the Kabbalists, there were also people working and making money, and

00:52:22.300 --> 00:52:28.300
tanning leather, and there were weavers, and there were...

00:52:28.300 --> 00:52:29.300
On an individual basis?

00:52:29.300 --> 00:52:30.300
No, no, yes.

00:52:30.300 --> 00:52:31.300
That was a political...

00:52:31.300 --> 00:52:32.300
Of course, of course.

00:52:32.300 --> 00:52:39.300
Now, when they came, these two settlers, they didn't settle the cities.

00:52:39.300 --> 00:52:41.300
They settled Kibbutzim.

00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:49.300
kibbutzim. There are no kibbutzim. Four letters to you outside the kibbutz. We care about

00:52:49.300 --> 00:52:57.300
ours. We take from others. We don't give to others. The most selfish organization that

00:52:57.300 --> 00:53:03.300
you, in the Jewish world, is the kibbutz. The people from the town, in the town you

00:53:03.300 --> 00:53:10.300
have a kind of civil relationship between the individuals. The kibbutz means four letters

00:53:10.300 --> 00:53:16.300
for you, take your money, for this were Jewish, like Timur men.

00:53:16.300 --> 00:53:22.300
But when he come to hell or so on, you get out from here, you see?

00:53:22.300 --> 00:53:31.300
Totally, absolutely selfish. And we were too much of a, too good of a people, you know?

00:53:31.300 --> 00:53:33.300
And we brought this stupidity.

00:53:33.300 --> 00:53:38.300
Yeah, but maybe we would have been good people in Spain or in Russia or in Israel.

00:53:38.300 --> 00:53:40.800
But in Israel, they're talking about the people in Israel.

00:53:40.800 --> 00:53:48.800
You think that the Hachamim in Israel, the Rishon Esion in Israel, he was a member by the way.

00:53:48.800 --> 00:53:52.800
This is what I want to publish by Eshat Hashem, maybe I publish it next year.

00:53:52.800 --> 00:53:55.800
I am all tied to the commentation.

00:53:55.800 --> 00:53:58.800
There were Jews in Israel, terrible intelligent Jews.

00:53:58.800 --> 00:54:03.300
Very, very intelligent, very educated, we can ask this all over the world.

00:54:03.300 --> 00:54:08.500
Now the Jews in Israel, I don't know if you know, I think it was in the First World War.

00:54:09.180 --> 00:54:14.560
The last battle of the First World War between the Turks and the British.

00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:16.000
You know where it was fought?

00:54:17.120 --> 00:54:17.560
What?

00:54:18.560 --> 00:54:19.000
No.

00:54:19.860 --> 00:54:20.900
It was in Israel.

00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:22.540
In Israel.

00:54:22.800 --> 00:54:24.280
That's where they fought.

00:54:25.040 --> 00:54:26.180
Before, what?

00:54:27.840 --> 00:54:30.080
They said they were on the way up to Damascus.

00:54:30.240 --> 00:54:31.500
They reached a fight.

00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:54.640
It was the area where they were fighting. Now, the Sephardic Jews in Israel, we have the documentation, contacted, they had a deal. America still was, until 1919, America still under Woodrow Wilson, America was neutral, didn't want to go to war.

00:54:54.640 --> 00:55:14.640
And so the combination was, Turks, the Turkish government was willing to surrender Palestine to the Americans in trust for the Jewish people rather than to, because they knew that they were going to lose the war.

00:55:14.640 --> 00:55:27.640
You know, and we have the documentation of the Americans at the time was a Jew, was a Secretary of State, Morgan Law, which was a Secretary of State, was a Jew.

00:55:27.640 --> 00:55:33.640
And Woodrow Wilson was very much interested because he wanted peace. He didn't want America to go into war.

00:55:33.640 --> 00:55:39.080
and they would take Israel, Palestine, in trust for the Jewish people.

00:55:39.080 --> 00:55:46.080
In other words, the Turks would surrender, would give Israel, Palestine to America in trust for the Jewish people.

00:55:46.080 --> 00:55:49.800
And that would be the end of the war.

00:55:49.800 --> 00:55:57.000
And that would be great for Turkey, because Turkey didn't want to continue fighting. They knew they lost.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:59.000
You know who opposed this?

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:12.000
Weissmann and Ben-Gurion. They wanted the Jews to receive Israel, not from the Turks, from the British.

00:56:12.000 --> 00:56:22.000
And, so it is very nice. I think that they have accepted the other plan. Six million Jews will not be killed in the war.

00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:30.000
So it's very interesting, they always tell you about the so-called positive parts of what these Zionists did at the beginning,

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:35.000
and so on, they're very beautiful, but they don't let you investigate the other things, you know.

00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:37.000
Is Zionism racism?

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:43.000
Well, it's a very nice question. I have a nice question. Listen to this.

00:56:43.000 --> 00:56:47.000
If I don't believe in the Christ, I don't believe the Christ is some stupidity.

00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:50.100
We were never in Sinai, we were never in Egypt as slaves.

00:56:50.100 --> 00:56:54.220
We have nothing in common spiritually or otherwise.

00:56:54.220 --> 00:56:58.440
And there's nothing in the future for us,

00:56:58.440 --> 00:57:00.300
which is common between me and you,

00:57:00.300 --> 00:57:01.460
so it's a little bit different.

00:57:01.460 --> 00:57:04.780
So what connects me to you?

00:57:04.780 --> 00:57:08.000
What connects me to you, me and you, to the land of Israel?

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:08.840
What?

00:57:09.980 --> 00:57:11.760
What, what is it?

00:57:11.760 --> 00:57:16.460
So something like they say in the language, Jewish blood.

00:57:16.460 --> 00:57:20.960
It sounds to me like racism, but I don't know, maybe somebody could explain to me.

00:57:20.960 --> 00:57:32.960
Maybe Yossi Sarit and Yossi Bein could tell me what is in common between Yossi Bein and my grandmother.

00:57:32.960 --> 00:57:38.960
I know there is a lot of common between me and his grandmother, because his grandmother believed in Torah,

00:57:38.960 --> 00:57:42.960
believed in Judaism, believed in God, believed in all those things that we believe in.

00:57:42.960 --> 00:57:45.960
We live in a time where we are special people with a special history.

00:57:45.960 --> 00:57:50.960
So I feel that I have a connection with Joseph Berlin's mother, the grandmother.

00:57:50.960 --> 00:57:55.960
But what is the solution between him and my grandmother?

00:57:55.960 --> 00:57:58.960
We are going to say, Jews what?

00:57:58.960 --> 00:58:03.960
But try to explain to me this. It sounds to me a little bit like racism.

00:58:03.960 --> 00:58:07.960
Yes. It sounds to me today a little bit like racism.

00:58:07.960 --> 00:58:14.960
No Torah, then you are racist.

00:58:14.960 --> 00:58:21.960
Not going to him. What makes him Jewish? I will consider him Jewish anytime.

00:58:21.960 --> 00:58:26.960
I will consider him 100%. Don't forget about it.

00:58:26.960 --> 00:58:31.960
And as I say, God gave the greatest punishment in the world to Yossi Sarif.

00:58:31.960 --> 00:58:36.960
God punished him in a horrible way. His son is religious.

00:58:36.960 --> 00:58:42.360
Yes? So that you can't say that this is not a pious one, all right?

00:58:42.360 --> 00:58:48.080
All right? So I have no problem with me from my point of view in Yosemite.

00:58:48.080 --> 00:58:51.580
I have no problem. I'm asking between him and my grandmother.

00:58:51.580 --> 00:58:56.080
I have no problem with me and his grandmother also. I have no problem at all.

00:58:56.080 --> 00:58:59.960
I, I, I, you know, no problem. But if you negate it around,

00:58:59.960 --> 00:59:05.720
then what is the, what factor

00:59:05.720 --> 00:59:08.920
is the uniting element among us.

00:59:08.920 --> 00:59:13.720
What is it?

00:59:13.720 --> 00:59:17.920
Jewish blood. It's just the Jewish blood. I don't know.

00:59:17.920 --> 00:59:21.720
They have to explain this to me.

00:59:21.720 --> 00:59:24.720
I understand that.

00:59:24.720 --> 00:59:27.720
What?

00:59:27.720 --> 00:59:30.720
It comes from German...

00:59:30.720 --> 00:59:33.720
I don't care what it is. The Germans,

00:59:33.720 --> 00:59:45.220
Germans, they're Germans, people don't understand. There are no free lunches in politics. Germans, they have their own philosophy, they have their own land and so on.

00:59:45.220 --> 01:00:01.320
That philosophy cannot be exported. You have to develop your own institutions. Now what is the basic value that we Jews have? It's a constitution called Torah.

01:00:01.320 --> 01:00:22.500
If you want to translate the Torah, the word Torah, in Spanish we call it Lel, in Greek Nomos, in Arabic Sharia, in English Law. It is the law of the Jewish people.

01:00:22.500 --> 01:00:26.500
democracy is the constitution of the Jewish people.

01:00:26.500 --> 01:00:30.500
So we have democracy, we cannot have Torah.

01:00:30.500 --> 01:00:34.500
Democracy cannot have a constitution?

01:00:38.500 --> 01:00:42.500
These people they speak about democracy, I don't know.

01:00:42.500 --> 01:00:46.500
They don't know what the word democracy is about. Think that democracy is to

01:00:46.500 --> 01:00:50.500
what is democracy? Democracy means

01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:55.180
that I can eat cheeseburgers. For this you don't need democracy. Eat it or don't eat it.

01:00:55.180 --> 01:01:00.180
You don't, no, that's not the political ideal of democracy.

01:01:00.180 --> 01:01:07.180
It's not just a cheeseburger.

01:01:07.180 --> 01:01:11.580
Eat cheeseburger or don't. It's not democracy.

01:01:11.580 --> 01:01:16.580
Major Savoy says, no, I'm an American. I could eat cheeseburger.

01:01:20.500 --> 01:01:40.500
I don't know, these people are really, they are losers, in Israeli I call it losers.

01:01:40.500 --> 01:01:47.500
There is nobody a greater loser than the State of Israel, won every single battle in the field,

01:01:47.500 --> 01:02:01.500
lost every single diplomatic encounter with the opposition. Every diplomatic enterprise of Israel ended in failure. These are losers.

01:02:01.500 --> 01:02:13.500
They are incompetent. They are mentally imbeciles. That's what they are. You know? There's nothing political about it. They're just stupid.

01:02:13.500 --> 01:02:22.500
It's stupid. You know, it's stupid. The only leader today in the Middle East is Arafat. He plays for them.

01:02:22.500 --> 01:02:35.500
I never saw a Hindu movie. I never saw a Hindu movie. But once I read, because I think the Hindu film industry is the largest in the world.

01:02:35.500 --> 01:02:40.500
Because after that, like a half a billion people will look into the movies.

01:02:40.500 --> 01:02:42.500
So how the movie goes?

01:02:42.500 --> 01:02:48.500
Mr. A wants to have a baby.

01:02:48.500 --> 01:02:52.500
Miss A, Miss B, right?

01:02:52.500 --> 01:02:57.500
So this and this one, they love each other, they're going to marry each other.

01:02:57.500 --> 01:03:02.500
But he or she did something that was misinterpreted by the other.

01:03:02.500 --> 01:03:04.320
So they have a fight, they break.

01:03:05.520 --> 01:03:08.480
Ten years hence, somebody explained to the other side,

01:03:08.820 --> 01:03:11.640
really, Mr. A. didn't want to say this,

01:03:11.740 --> 01:03:12.880
wanted to say the other word.

01:03:13.540 --> 01:03:16.560
Oh, yes, now that's time to reunite.

01:03:17.160 --> 01:03:17.420
Yes?

01:03:17.860 --> 01:03:19.440
And now when she tried to reunite,

01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:23.000
he or she does something that the other guy misinterpreted.

01:03:24.160 --> 01:03:24.840
This is it?

01:03:25.280 --> 01:03:26.060
We break again.

01:03:27.000 --> 01:03:28.880
And then, continues like this,

01:03:28.880 --> 01:03:30.600
they move for two, three, four hours.

01:03:30.600 --> 01:03:39.840
And at the end, after 50 years, they're all both old, and he, again, does something.

01:03:41.180 --> 01:03:44.800
And we don't know whether she is going to interpret it this way or the other.

01:03:44.880 --> 01:03:45.740
It's at the end of the movie.

01:03:46.760 --> 01:03:49.020
Do you know how to translate this in real terms?

01:03:50.460 --> 01:03:51.520
Arafat and Perez.

01:03:53.380 --> 01:03:55.900
That is the couple that met 50 years ago.

01:03:56.820 --> 01:03:59.920
They are, each one misinterprets the other.

01:03:59.920 --> 01:04:04.700
But still maybe, maybe, maybe at the end they're going to hold this together.

01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:05.880
Yes?

01:04:06.340 --> 01:04:09.500
And we're going to see the end of the film, yes?

01:04:10.060 --> 01:04:14.520
Them holding hands in a bright new Middle East.

01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:15.760
Or maybe not.

01:04:17.140 --> 01:04:19.200
That is the Israeli politics.

01:04:22.620 --> 01:04:29.740
In a democracy, unfortunately, the leaders are limited to what they can do.

01:04:29.920 --> 01:04:34.920
depending on where their constituents are at.

01:04:36.020 --> 01:04:38.220
They can't get too far ahead of them.

01:04:38.220 --> 01:04:40.900
If they do, they're not empowering.

01:04:41.780 --> 01:04:46.640
So I don't think it's necessarily the leadership

01:04:46.640 --> 01:04:48.080
all the time.

01:04:48.080 --> 01:04:51.400
Sometimes it's the problem of the people themselves.

01:04:51.400 --> 01:04:52.600
This is partially true.

01:04:52.600 --> 01:04:55.280
But in Israel we do not have a,

01:04:55.280 --> 01:04:56.840
you don't vote for nobody.

01:04:56.840 --> 01:04:58.380
You have only two parties

01:04:58.380 --> 01:05:04.380
nobody could touch those parties. There are two parties and they nominate whomever they want to nominate.

01:05:04.380 --> 01:05:13.380
And you have the choice between two bad things, two rotten apples. And this is the great thing, choose one.

01:05:13.380 --> 01:05:18.380
But you can have your own candidate, you can have the other one. It's impossible, the system does not allow it.

01:05:18.380 --> 01:05:24.380
But whoever, whether they had that system or not, whoever would be in the leadership position?

01:05:24.380 --> 01:05:25.680
They do whatever they want to.

01:05:25.800 --> 01:05:29.100
They don't have representative democracy.

01:05:29.240 --> 01:05:30.680
They have parliamentary democracy,

01:05:30.900 --> 01:05:37.500
which allows the central party system to tell everybody what to do.

01:05:37.500 --> 01:05:40.920
If you had independence in, say, Becimish,

01:05:41.080 --> 01:05:43.000
or in these type of places where this is happening,

01:05:43.380 --> 01:05:46.640
then they would have grassroots democracy,

01:05:46.940 --> 01:05:48.940
and this is what the parties are afraid of.

01:05:49.220 --> 01:05:50.240
There really is no democracy.

01:05:51.900 --> 01:05:53.160
We don't elect our minister.

01:05:53.160 --> 01:05:57.160
You don't have to vote for one party or the other.

01:05:57.160 --> 01:06:02.160
Now the police, at one time they had the possibility for, well, Netanyahu was in power,

01:06:02.160 --> 01:06:05.160
that you could vote directly for the parliamentarians. Now you cannot do it no more.

01:06:05.160 --> 01:06:10.160
They stopped it. Because Barmendan, the good people vote without the parties.

01:06:10.160 --> 01:06:14.160
Then how are you going to get the ball to your best girlfriend?

01:06:14.160 --> 01:06:16.160
They don't do that anymore. I didn't know.

01:06:16.160 --> 01:06:18.160
Yeah, of course not. I don't know.

01:06:18.160 --> 01:06:28.300
And also you have no freedom of speech because the media, you know, say a person like Rafa El-Sef,

01:06:29.140 --> 01:06:33.180
he cannot establish, he cannot have his own station, radio station.

01:06:34.120 --> 01:06:34.560
You cannot.

01:06:35.240 --> 01:06:37.840
You cannot have legal, they will not give you a license.

01:06:38.460 --> 01:06:45.040
You cannot, of course, have your, there are only two TV stations, and both of them are government controlled.

01:06:45.040 --> 01:06:45.800
You cannot establish.

01:06:45.800 --> 01:06:49.740
You cannot have your own TV station.

01:06:49.840 --> 01:06:51.880
Does he have his own thing?

01:06:52.120 --> 01:06:53.420
It's not legal?

01:06:53.660 --> 01:06:53.960
What?

01:06:55.400 --> 01:06:56.420
It's called pirate.

01:06:56.780 --> 01:06:57.320
Pirate.

01:06:57.700 --> 01:06:58.900
No, no.

01:06:59.580 --> 01:07:02.020
Doesn't he have his broadcast on state radio?

01:07:02.340 --> 01:07:02.780
That's private.

01:07:04.480 --> 01:07:06.240
It's private.

01:07:06.480 --> 01:07:07.220
It has a satellite.

01:07:07.980 --> 01:07:09.960
It doesn't use the usual.

01:07:10.360 --> 01:07:12.900
You have to be a member of that, pay money on all of this,

01:07:12.900 --> 01:07:13.820
and you get it.

01:07:13.820 --> 01:07:15.820
It's not a radio from the...

01:07:15.820 --> 01:07:17.820
It's not I-107.

01:07:17.820 --> 01:07:21.820
I-107 is considered as a pirate station.

01:07:21.820 --> 01:07:22.820
Yes.

01:07:22.820 --> 01:07:26.820
They go in and they take the mother's shoulder and they open the door.

01:07:26.820 --> 01:07:35.820
I'm sorry, I just want to say, now, if you're a terrorist, yes, they give you the best platform in the world.

01:07:35.820 --> 01:07:43.820
the more time allotted to the terrorists than to the ONSF.

01:07:43.820 --> 01:07:52.820
I don't agree with the political ideas of the ONSF, but why should the terrorists have a better platform than the ONSF? Why?

01:07:52.820 --> 01:07:55.820
What's that?

01:07:55.820 --> 01:07:59.820
The television, they ask the question, they interview, and so on.

01:07:59.820 --> 01:08:07.820
The media would provide them access to interviews and through allowing them to make public statements, then they would figure out what they never said.

01:08:07.820 --> 01:08:16.820
By the way, I want to say something very interesting. They were wonderful, the Arabs. I was like, they're so nice people, they're really nice people.

01:08:16.820 --> 01:08:22.820
Just give them a little bit more of that. And they're wonderful people and they're not like the Nazis.

01:08:22.820 --> 01:08:24.220
But you know, interesting thing.

01:08:25.160 --> 01:08:30.260
I never heard of Nazis drinking Jewish blood.

01:08:30.360 --> 01:08:34.400
You know when the Arabs kill Jews, they take the blood and they drink it?

01:08:37.300 --> 01:08:40.060
They paint themselves with the blood of the Jews?

01:08:43.500 --> 01:08:46.040
And we want to make peace with them.

01:08:47.280 --> 01:08:52.660
Just give them a little bit more land and one or two pints of Jewish blood for breakfast.

01:08:52.660 --> 01:08:59.660
every morning. This is the people we want to make peace with them? Is this hypocrisy?

01:09:00.980 --> 01:09:07.900
In what way are they better than Eichmann? In what way? Well, they don't kill 60 million

01:09:07.900 --> 01:09:10.900
Jews because they cannot physically, they don't have the means.

01:09:10.900 --> 01:09:17.900
Do you think if we had a system of democracy there like we have in the United States, it

01:09:17.900 --> 01:09:19.900
would make a difference?

01:09:19.900 --> 01:09:24.220
Of course. One thing that Ori told me, and she has a great idea,

01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:27.820
first of all, Americans should go to Israel,

01:09:28.360 --> 01:09:33.820
and should have the Anglo-Saxon Israeli political party.

01:09:36.040 --> 01:09:37.680
I mean, she's right.

01:09:39.140 --> 01:09:45.500
It has to be the political mind of a true democracy,

01:09:45.500 --> 01:09:48.900
which is England is a true democracy, America is a true democracy,

01:09:48.900 --> 01:09:49.900
You see, Canada...

01:09:49.900 --> 01:09:51.900
All of that is a great old stuff.

01:09:51.900 --> 01:10:02.900
Yeah, but you see, David Nassi, somebody from Suriname, he said, well, you know, America, is it...

01:10:02.900 --> 01:10:07.900
or King Solomon. He says, they're very intelligent.

01:10:07.900 --> 01:10:23.900
If there is such thing as an ethical, national ethical values, it makes a difference whether this government is called a monarchy or a republic or what's called this.

01:10:23.900 --> 01:10:33.900
It would work, but if there are no basic moral values, like in the people, call it what you will, the government is not going to work.

01:10:33.900 --> 01:10:47.900
So, whether it's a parliamentary or a non-parliamentary democracy, the most important thing, are there any common values that unite us?

01:10:47.900 --> 01:10:53.900
Traditionally there were, and we call those Torah. They were common values.

01:10:53.900 --> 01:10:58.900
So, how the government is going to be, that's why I told you what kind of government we should have.

01:10:58.900 --> 01:11:02.400
Because it's secondary, it's what we want.

01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:05.400
Maybe we want to have a republic, but that's not important.

01:11:05.400 --> 01:11:11.400
You know, the important thing is, are we united by common values?

01:11:11.400 --> 01:11:15.400
That's the important thing. The other things are secondary.

01:11:15.400 --> 01:11:17.400
You know, say...

01:11:17.400 --> 01:11:21.400
How could we become united by common values?

01:11:21.400 --> 01:11:23.400
Well, we have the Torah.

01:11:23.400 --> 01:11:25.400
We don't play it in Israel, unfortunately.

01:11:25.400 --> 01:11:32.400
by force. In Israel there is a lot of coercion and manipulation and intimidation going on.

01:11:32.400 --> 01:11:39.400
And it's unfortunate. But I do believe that, it's a question of personal belief, Am Yisrael

01:11:39.400 --> 01:11:46.400
is eternal and eventually we're going to overcome these problems. But if we're going to overcome

01:11:46.400 --> 01:11:51.400
these problems, it's not going to be because some of the politicians make Teshuvah. One

01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:59.240
One of the points that we have in Rosh Hashanah is in Rosh Hashanah we have Sifrei Chaim v'sifremetiv.

01:12:00.420 --> 01:12:09.000
In other words, because the Torah is the first system in which organizes freedom, individual freedom,

01:12:09.620 --> 01:12:11.460
means individual responsibility.

01:12:12.980 --> 01:12:21.120
So, to the fault, because we have individual responsibility, we have to render account of our behavior.

01:12:21.400 --> 01:12:29.400
But also, it's not only individually, but also as a member of a community or of a nation.

01:12:29.400 --> 01:12:34.400
So we are judged individually, and the nation is judged collectively.

01:12:34.400 --> 01:12:38.400
So individually I may be the greatest person in the world,

01:12:38.400 --> 01:12:44.400
God will give me the best penthouse with a beautiful view in Al-Ahmadbah,

01:12:44.400 --> 01:12:49.400
but in Al-Ahmadzeh I have to suffer with all my friends.

01:12:49.400 --> 01:12:59.740
if the collective, collective Israel, Knesset Israel is at fault, you know.

01:13:00.640 --> 01:13:04.800
And so therefore, these two dimensions are in which they are now, you know.

01:13:05.380 --> 01:13:08.080
Sefer Haim, Sefer Metim, you know.

01:13:09.340 --> 01:13:14.400
We pray for Am Yisrael, for the nation of Israel, you know.

01:13:14.400 --> 01:13:32.000
And we want the nation as a nation to receive the blessings of God and so on. And there is what Rabbi Ullah Bivas in Ar HaKhamim and I say always in my writings and so on, we call it political deshuva.

01:13:32.000 --> 01:13:39.680
to make the has of each one as a nation you know and to say enough golden stupid

01:13:39.680 --> 01:13:48.860
jokes yes we don't want the egg in to do to finish with this and then getting

01:13:48.860 --> 01:14:01.440
late a great ha ha this was a we were fortunate we had great coming one of

01:14:01.440 --> 01:14:11.240
them is Rabbi Shaul, Shaul David Mortega. He was from Amsterdam. He was the Rabbi of Amsterdam.

01:14:14.420 --> 01:14:20.180
Intelligent, very intelligent Rabbi. And he says something to the effect that I translated

01:14:20.180 --> 01:14:24.540
my own views are the following.

01:14:25.260 --> 01:14:29.200
We have Esav, and we have Yaakov.

01:14:31.060 --> 01:14:33.420
Esav, he was a hunter.

01:14:33.700 --> 01:14:34.380
He's a zayt.

01:14:36.000 --> 01:14:36.900
He's a zayt.

01:14:38.940 --> 01:14:41.700
Yaakov, he's a shepherd.

01:14:42.900 --> 01:14:42.760
He was a shepherd.

01:14:42.920 --> 01:14:44.120
Yeshuvahalim means a shepherd.

01:14:45.660 --> 01:14:47.840
And therefore we know the whole struggle.

01:14:47.840 --> 01:15:03.840
And at the end, Yaakov, successful or triumphed, or whatever it is. He has a very, very intelligent, very astute derashah.

01:15:03.840 --> 01:15:19.840
He says there are only two kinds of political leaders. One political leader is the person of Esau. He is a hunter. He is a hunter.

01:15:19.840 --> 01:15:33.840
He knows how to express rhetoric, how people chanted what he says and so on.

01:15:33.840 --> 01:15:38.840
But he is a hunter. He hunts you.

01:15:38.840 --> 01:15:44.840
And he plays with the other, this and that.

01:15:44.840 --> 01:15:53.840
It's always who is Lashon. He's having fights with the others in the Tat, in order to get the other things.

01:15:53.840 --> 01:15:55.840
This is one kind of political leader.

01:15:55.840 --> 01:15:57.840
Esad.

01:15:57.840 --> 01:16:03.840
And then you have another kind of leader, that is Yaakov, which is a shepherd.

01:16:03.840 --> 01:16:12.840
He takes care of every single sheep and guides them to the proper green pastures, waters and so on.

01:16:12.840 --> 01:16:21.840
and it's protected the people. So we have the ideal political leader for us is Yaakov.

01:16:21.840 --> 01:16:29.840
Unfortunately, in modern times, the Assad figure becomes more and more dominant.

01:16:29.840 --> 01:16:36.840
The leader becomes the man who knows how to hunt people with his mouth, his side with his...

01:16:36.840 --> 01:16:55.340
.

